    "review_conclusions": [
      "CreateEventW FALSE selects auto-reset; existing-name state/type/ACL are not replaced, so a newly owned protocol rejects every collision.",
      "Auto-reset signals persist without a waiter and release one waiter. Repeated SetEvent does not count pulses; exactly one outstanding action is required.",
      "Use only role-required EVENT_MODIFY_STATE/SYNCHRONIZE handle rights, protected current-user local-session names and disabled inheritance. This is trusted-worker containment, not hostile same-user isolation.",
      "Never close a waited handle while waiting; current source/peer lifetime leases remain owned until confirmed retirement.",
      "TerminateProcess requests I/O cancellation asynchronously; terminated kernel objects remain referenced by open handles. Actual process and supervisor exit remain separate gates."
    ],
